📊 Customer Intelligence & Purchase Prediction System

📝 Project Overview

This project is an end-to-end Machine Learning solution designed to analyze customer purchasing behavior, segment high-value customers, and predict future transactions. Built using the UCI "Online Retail II" dataset (wholesale novelty distribution), the system identifies which customers are most likely to make a purchase in the next 30 days, empowering marketing teams to optimize their retention campaigns.

The project encompasses a complete data science lifecycle, from raw data preprocessing and feature engineering to model deployment via a RESTful API and an interactive Streamlit web dashboard.

🚀 Key Features

Data Pipeline & Feature Engineering: Cleans an 800k+ row dataset, handles missing values, and engineers robust RFM (Recency, Frequency, Monetary) behavioral features.

Machine Learning (Purchase Prediction): Evaluates 5 classification models (Dummy, Logistic Regression, Decision Tree, Random Forest, Gradient Boosting) using advanced metrics (PR-AUC, Precision@100). The winning Logistic Regression model balances recall and precision to catch actual returning buyers.

Unsupervised Customer Segmentation: Uses log-transformation and K-Means Clustering to mathematically group customers into 4 distinct segments, successfully identifying the "Champion" VIP buyers.

Production REST API: A fully functional FastAPI web server with Pydantic data validation, delivering live predictions via a /predict endpoint.

Interactive Dashboard: A sleek Streamlit web application featuring Business Analytics KPIs, dynamic clustering visuals, and a 30-day prediction simulator for non-technical stakeholders.

Automated Testing: Implementation of pytest to ensure API reliability and exact JSON schema matching.

📂 Repository Structure

customer-intelligence-ml/
│
├── api/                    # Production FastAPI application
│   ├── main.py             # API endpoints (/health, /predict)
│   └── test_main.py        # Automated Pytest scripts
│
├── dashboard/              # Interactive Streamlit frontend
│   └── app.py              # Dashboard UI and data visualizations
│
├── Data/                   # Raw and processed datasets
│   └── raw_data.xlsx       # (Not included in repo due to size)
│
├── notebooks/              # Initial Jupyter notebooks for EDA 
|   └── 01_data_understanding.ipynb
│
├── src/                    # Core Machine Learning pipeline scripts
│   ├── data_preprocessing.py
│   ├── feature_engineering.py
│   ├── train.py            # Script to train, compare and evaluate model
│   ├── clustering.py       # K-Means segmentation logic
│   └── save_model.py       # Script to export the final .pkl model
│
├── production_model.pkl    # Serialized Logistic Regression model
└── README.md


🛠️ Tech Stack

Language: Python 3

Data Manipulation: Pandas, NumPy

Machine Learning: Scikit-learn (Logistic Regression, K-Means, RandomForest)

API & Deployment: FastAPI, Uvicorn, Pydantic

Frontend Dashboard: Streamlit, Matplotlib, Seaborn

Testing: Pytest, Httpx

⚙️ How to Run the Project

1. Setup Environment

Ensure you have Python installed, then create and activate a virtual environment:

python -m venv .venv
# On Windows:
.venv\Scripts\activate
# On Mac/Linux:
source .venv/bin/activate


Install required dependencies:

pip install pandas numpy scikit-learn matplotlib seaborn fastapi uvicorn pydantic joblib pytest httpx streamlit


2. Run the REST API

To launch the FastAPI server and access the Swagger UI documentation:

uvicorn api.main:app --reload


Visit http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs to test the endpoints interactively.

3. Run the Interactive Dashboard

To launch the Streamlit frontend application:

streamlit run dashboard/app.py


A new browser tab will open displaying the Customer Intelligence Hub.

4. Run Automated Tests

To verify the health and schema of the API using Pytest:

pytest api/test_main.py -v


🏆 Business Impact

By deploying this system, businesses can confidently identify which customers are on the verge of returning and which "Champions" generate the most revenue. This allows for targeted, cost-effective marketing strategies, reducing promotional waste while maximizing customer lifetime value.